1re6img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le16ob01re6img01.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 4, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le16ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn4le16ob01re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn4le16ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Yesterday, I visited the Great Wall of China.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn4le16ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Here's some history about this structure.  The wall wasn't built in one generation. Many generations of builders helped to create it. Builders in the 5th century BC started the Great Wall to keep out the tribes who lived north of China.", "id": 2, "time": "4500", "image": "engenn4le16ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The first step was to connect the existing walls of Chinese states. The wall that stands today was built by emperors of the Ming Dynasty between the 14th and the 17th centuries.", "id": 3, "time": "22500", "image": "engenn4le16ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "It's about 55 miles from Beijing. To walk from one end of the Great Wall to the other is 4,000 miles! It runs from western China to the Yellow Sea.", "id": 4, "time": "36000", "image": "engenn4le16ob01re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "There are many towers along the wall. Guards used to stand in these towers, watching and sending signals back to the capital city.", "id": 5, "time": "50000", "image": "engenn4le16ob01re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}]}], "type": "sena"}